<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inzak</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Enzak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Inzak, also written Enzak, was the chief god of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilmun">Dilmun</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> civilisation centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a>. Inscriptions from Bahrain and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/failaka-island">Failaka</a> name him, and in the Sumerian myth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enki">Enki</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ninhursag">Ninhursag</a> he is appointed lord of Dilmun. His consort was the goddess Meskilak.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inzak.jpg" alt="Inzak" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Droodkin · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Durand_Stone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
